.TH STORMBYTE-DATACENTER 1 "August 2026" "StormByte" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
StormByte-DataCenter \- disk inventory, SES IDENT LEDs, SCSI format, ZFS and Btrfs helpers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B StormByte-DataCenter
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fISUBCOMMAND\fR...] [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B StormByte-DataCenter
is a unified CLI for SCSI/SAS/SATA disk inventory, enclosure IDENT LED control,
SCSI FORMAT UNIT, and common ZFS/Btrfs operations in a multipath-capable environment.

Disk identity arguments (device names, WWN, SCSI or ATA by-id names, including
full
.I /dev/disk/by-id/...
paths) are normalized to a stable identity key (real WWN hex, or a synthetic
key for disks without WWN such as many system SATA drives). Block I/O uses a
resolved
.B access path
(multipath mapper preferred when raw by-id nodes are blocked by multipath).

The script loads shared libraries from the same directory as the executable
first, then from
.IR /lib/StormByte/
.RB ( functions.sh
and
.BR datacenter.sh ).

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B POOL
Default ZFS pool name (default:
.BR StormDataCenter ).
.TP
.B SMARTCTL_TIMEOUT
Timeout in seconds for
.B smartctl
invocations (default:
.BR 10 ).

.SH DEVICE ARGUMENTS
Where a device is accepted, the following forms are equivalent when unique:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.IR sdX
or
.I /dev/sdX
.IP \(bu 2
.IR wwn-0x...
or
.I /dev/disk/by-id/wwn-0x...
.IP \(bu 2
.IR scsi-...
or
.I /dev/disk/by-id/scsi-...
.IP \(bu 2
.IR ata-...
or
.I /dev/disk/by-id/ata-...
.RE
Identity is always resolved first; privileged I/O uses the best usable access
path. SES LED control uses enclosure sysfs matching by SAS/WWN prefix for disks
with a real hex WWN only (system SATA without WWN show Enclosure/LED as N/A).

.SH PRIVILEGES
Operations that need elevated rights invoke
.B sudo
automatically when the process is not already root. The user does not need to
re-run the entire CLI under
.BR sudo .

Elevated rights are used for:
.BR "disk list -v" ,
.BR "disk health" ,
.BR "disk info" ,
.BR "disk format" ,
.BR "led on" ,
.BR "led off" ,
.BR "led blink" ,
.BR "disk zfs scrub" ,
.BR "disk zfs scrub stop" ,
.BR "disk btrfs scrub start" ,
.BR "disk btrfs scrub cancel" .

.SH COMMANDS
.SS help
.TP
.B help
Show the built-in help message and exit.

.SS disk list
.TP
.B disk list\fR [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fIdevice\fR]
List disks (all
.B sd*
nodes), deduplicated by identity, ordered by enclosure/slot when available.
Without
.B \-v
columns include Device, Identifiers, Vendor, Model, FW, Pool membership and LED.
With
.B \-v
also Enclosure, SMART, Temperature, Link, Health and Path.
Uses
.B smartctl
via
.B sudo
when
.B \-v
is set.

.SS disk health
.TP
.B disk health\fR [\fIdevice\fR]
Compact SMART/health summary for one disk or all disks
.RB ( smartctl
via
.BR sudo ).

.SS disk info
.TP
.B disk info\fR \fIdevice\fR
Formatted SMART-oriented summary for a single disk (not a raw smartctl dump):
identity, access path, enclosure, pool membership, overall SMART, temperature
and selected error counters.
Device is mandatory.

.SS disk format
.TP
.B disk format\fR \fIdevice\fR [\fB\-\-progress\fR]
Perform a SCSI FORMAT UNIT using
.B sg_format
from
.B sg3_utils
on the resolved access path.
Fails if
.B sg_format
is missing or if the device cannot be formatted that way.
.B \-\-progress
requests progress reporting from
.BR sg_format .
The operation is destructive and requires typing
.B YES
to confirm.
Runs via
.B sudo
when not root.

.SS disk zfs
If a named pool does not exist, the tool reports an error itself (it does not
rely on opaque
.B zpool
messages alone).
.TP
.B disk zfs status\fR [\fB\-v\fR] [\fIpool\fR]
Show
.B zpool status
(default pool from
.BR POOL ).
With
.B \-v
uses
.BR "zpool status -v" .
Does not require elevation.
.TP
.B disk zfs list
List pools and datasets. Does not require elevation.
.TP
.B disk zfs iostat\fR [\fIinterval\fR]
.B zpool iostat
for the default pool. Does not require elevation.
.TP
.B disk zfs events
.B zpool events
for the default pool. Does not require elevation.
.TP
.B disk zfs scrub
Start a scrub on the default pool (via
.BR sudo ).
.TP
.B disk zfs scrub stop
Stop a scrub on the default pool (via
.BR sudo ).

.SS disk btrfs
Non-btrfs paths are rejected with a clear error. Listing skips non-btrfs mounts.
.TP
.B disk btrfs status\fR [\fIpath\fR]
Filesystem show/usage for a btrfs path (default
.IR / ).
.TP
.B disk btrfs list
Detected btrfs filesystems and subvolumes on btrfs mounts only.
.TP
.B disk btrfs df\fR [\fIpath\fR]
.B btrfs filesystem df .
.TP
.B disk btrfs device\fR [\fIpath\fR]
Device usage summary for a btrfs path.
.TP
.B disk btrfs scrub start\fR [\fIpath\fR]
Start scrub (via
.BR sudo ).
.TP
.B disk btrfs scrub status\fR [\fIpath\fR]
Scrub status.
.TP
.B disk btrfs scrub cancel\fR [\fIpath\fR]
Cancel scrub (via
.BR sudo ).

.SS led
.TP
.B led on\fR [\fIdevice\fR]
Turn IDENT LED on for one disk or all enclosure disks (via
.BR sudo ).
.TP
.B led off\fR [\fIdevice\fR]
Turn IDENT LED off for one disk or all enclosure disks (via
.BR sudo ).
.TP
.B led show\fR [\fIdevice\fR]
Show IDENT LED state (table ordered by enclosure/slot when listing all).
Does not require elevation.
.TP
.B led blink\fR \fIdevice\fR [\fIseconds\fR]
Turn LED on, wait (default 30 seconds), turn LED off.
Device is mandatory.
Uses
.BR sudo .

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
StormByte-DataCenter disk list
StormByte-DataCenter disk list -v
StormByte-DataCenter disk health
StormByte-DataCenter disk info wwn-0x5000cca03e7ce8f8
StormByte-DataCenter disk info /dev/disk/by-id/scsi-35000c500566d10c3
StormByte-DataCenter disk format scsi-35000c500566d10c3 --progress
StormByte-DataCenter led show
StormByte-DataCenter led blink sda 15
StormByte-DataCenter disk zfs status -v
POOL=Other StormByte-DataCenter disk zfs scrub
StormByte-DataCenter disk btrfs status /
.fi

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
Error (invalid arguments, missing pool, non-btrfs path, format failure,
missing tools, cancelled confirmation, etc.)

.SH FILES
.TP
.I functions.sh
Shared StormByte helpers. Looked up next to the script, then
.IR /lib/StormByte/functions.sh .
.TP
.I datacenter.sh
Disk/WWN/SES/multipath helpers. Looked up next to the script, then
.IR /lib/StormByte/datacenter.sh .

.SH NOTES
- Incorrect commands print a short error and accepted syntax, not the full help.
- Multipath may block opening some by-id nodes; those names remain valid as
  identity because access is resolved separately.
- Enclosure LED operations require SES sysfs
  .RB ( /sys/class/enclosure )
  and a real WWN-based identity.
- .B disk format
  depends on
  .B sg_format
  from
  .BR sg3_utils .

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smartctl (8),
.BR sg_format (8),
.BR zpool (8),
.BR zfs (8),
.BR btrfs (8),
.BR multipath (8),
.BR lsscsi (8)

